     aatthh33kkffww — download firmware for Atheros AR3011/AR3012 Bluetooth USB de‐
     vices

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aatthh33kkffww [--DDII] --dd _d_e_v_i_c_e___n_a_m_e --ff _f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e___p_a_t_h
     aatthh33kkffww --hh

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aatthh33kkffww utility downloads the specified firmware file to the speci‐
     fied ugen(4) device.

     This utility will _o_n_l_y work with Atheros AR3011 and AR3012 chip based
     Bluetooth USB devices.  The identification is currently based on USB ven‐
     dor ID/product ID pair.  The vendor ID should be 0x0cf3
     (USB_VENDOR_ATHEROS2) and the product ID should be one of the supported
     devices.

     Firmware files are available in the linux-firmware RPM.

     The aatthh33kkffww utility will query the device to determine which firmware im‐
     age and board configuration to load in at runtime.

     The options are as follows:

     --DD                Enable verbose debugging.

     --dd _d_e_v_i_c_e___n_a_m_e    Specify ugen(4) device name.

     --ff _f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e___p_a_t_h  Specify the directory containing the firmware files to
                       search and upload.

     --hh                Display usage message and exit.

     --II                Enable informational debugging.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The aatthh33kkffww utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

